## Enhancement

Related issue: #53827, Index Merge Reader has the same issue too.

### 1. Minimal reproduce step (Required)

<!-- a step by step guide for reproducing the bug. -->

```sql
drop table if exists t;
create table t (id int key auto_increment, b int, c int, index idx1 (b), index idx2(c));
insert into t () values (), (), (), (), (), (), (), ();
insert into t (b) select b from t;
insert into t (b) select b from t;
insert into t (b) select b from t;
insert into t (b) select b from t;
insert into t (b) select b from t;
insert into t (b) select b from t;
insert into t (b) select b from t;
update t set b = id, c = id;

-- set following variables to default value. 
set @@tidb_enable_paging=1;
set @@tidb_min_paging_size=128;
set @@tidb_max_chunk_size=1024;

explain analyze select /*+ USE_INDEX_MERGE(t, idx1, idx2) */ * from t where b > 0 or c > 0;
```

### 2. What did you see instead (Required)

```sql
> explain analyze select /*+ USE_INDEX_MERGE(t, idx1, idx2) */ * from t where b > 0 or c > 0;
+---------------------------+---------+---------+-----------+------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------+---------+------+
| id                        | estRows | actRows | task      | access object          | execution info                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          | operator info                                  | memory  | disk |
+---------------------------+---------+---------+-----------+------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------+---------+------+
| IndexMerge_8              | 5555.56 | 1024    | root      |                        | time:2.83ms, loops:2, RU:4.930075, index_task:{fetch_handle:3.634626ms, merge:143.416µs}, table_task:{num:1, concurrency:5, fetch_row:598.25µs, wait_time:2.159291ms}                                                                                                                                                                   | type: union                                    | 71.0 KB | N/A  |
| ├─IndexRangeScan_5(Build) | 3333.33 | 1024    | cop[tikv] | table:t, index:idx1(b) | time:1.83ms, loops:2, cop_task: {num: 4, max: 836.1µs, min: 85.3µs, avg: 431.1µs, p95: 836.1µs, copr_cache_hit_ratio: 0.00, build_task_duration: 39.2µs, max_distsql_concurrency: 1}, rpc_info:{Cop:{num_rpc:4, total_time:1.68ms}}, tikv_task:{proc max:752.2µs, min:73.1µs, avg: 398.6µs, p80:752.2µs, p95:752.2µs, iters:0, tasks:4} | range:(0,+inf], keep order:false, stats:pseudo | N/A     | N/A  |
| ├─IndexRangeScan_6(Build) | 3333.33 | 1024    | cop[tikv] | table:t, index:idx2(c) | time:1.76ms, loops:2, cop_task: {num: 4, max: 835.9µs, min: 78.5µs, avg: 412.3µs, p95: 835.9µs, copr_cache_hit_ratio: 0.00, build_task_duration: 46.7µs, max_distsql_concurrency: 1}, rpc_info:{Cop:{num_rpc:4, total_time:1.6ms}}, tikv_task:{proc max:754.8µs, min:68.1µs, avg: 380.2µs, p80:754.8µs, p95:754.8µs, iters:0, tasks:4}  | range:(0,+inf], keep order:false, stats:pseudo | N/A     | N/A  |
| └─TableRowIDScan_7(Probe) | 5555.56 | 1024    | cop[tikv] | table:t                | time:480.3µs, loops:2, cop_task: {num: 1, max: 430.1µs, proc_keys: 0, copr_cache_hit_ratio: 0.00, build_task_duration: 9.58µs, max_distsql_concurrency: 1}, rpc_info:{Cop:{num_rpc:1, total_time:420µs}}, tikv_task:{time:403.2µs, loops:0}                                                                                             | keep order:false, stats:pseudo                 | N/A     | N/A  |
+---------------------------+---------+---------+-----------+------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------+---------+------+
```

Attention, `IndexRangeScan` sends 4 cop RPC to scan index.

```sql
IndexRangeScan_5(Build) | ... | table:t, index:idx1(b) | ... cop_task: {num: 4, ...}, rpc_info:{Cop:{num_rpc:4, ...
IndexRangeScan_6(Build) | ... | table:t, index:idx2(c) | ... cop_task: {num: 4, ...}, rpc_info:{Cop:{num_rpc:4, ...
```


### 3. What did you expect to see?

`IndexRangeScan` only send 1 RPC.

```sql
IndexRangeScan_5(Build) | ... | table:t, index:idx1(b) | ... cop_task: {num: 1, ...}, rpc_info:{Cop:{num_rpc:1, ...
IndexRangeScan_6(Build) | ... | table:t, index:idx2(c) | ... cop_task: {num: 1, ...}, rpc_info:{Cop:{num_rpc:1, ...
```

